1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:05,080
Coach: And reach and stretch and grab those grapes,

2
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:07,789
and punch that guy right in the face.

3
00:00:07,789 --> 00:00:09,793
Carol: Grade A students shouldn't have to take gym.

4
00:00:09,793 --> 00:00:13,803
Debbie: Oh, yeah Carol. Guys really go for a curvy brain.

5
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:17,380
Shelly: If it weren't for my shapely thighs, where would I be?

6
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:22,200
Carol: Name just one serious successful woman who worries about the shape

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:22,812
of her thighs?

8
00:00:22,812 --> 00:00:23,814
Shelly: Evana White.

9
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:26,460
Carol: Oh why, oh why didn't I think of her?

10
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,827
Principle: Attention people, this is your principle, Mr. Dewitt speaking.

11
00:00:30,827 --> 00:00:33,832
Girls: Wooooh!

12
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:39,980
Principle: Point it at my face. There we go. Good morning, students.

13
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:47,060
Yes, it's me. Coming to your via the all new Dewey High school Pa system

14
00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:51,300
Hooter vision. Your parents tax dollars at work.

15
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:52,880
Carol: This is like something out of Nineteen Eighty Four.

16
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:56,820
Principle: The homecoming dance is only two days away,

17
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:59,440
and the decorating committee still needs help.

18
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:03,380
Contact Bucky Kneehowser if you can donate any of the following decorative

19
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:08,860
items; balloons, streamers, slap shoes, chaps, whips, handcuffs...

20
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:13,600
ok forget this item. And I'd like to see Bucky Kneehowser in my office PDQ.

21
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:16,380
And now the big news.

22
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:19,800
The candidates who you have selected for homecoming king and queen.

23
00:01:19,901 --> 00:01:22,910
Girls: Woooo!

24
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:28,720
Principle: I get tingles too. Estelle, the envelope, please.

25
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:30,922
Debbie: It's just like the Academy awards.

26
00:01:30,922 --> 00:01:34,928
Carol: Oh yeah, will Rob Lowe be nominated, or passed over for yet another year?

27
00:01:34,928 --> 00:01:35,931
Shelly: Exactly.

28
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:39,700
Carol: Can you guys hear yourselves, you act like this is important.

29
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:41,520
Debbie: Oh and I suppose you're above all this?

30
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:43,920
Carol: This is merely an affirmation of a social order,

31
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:46,760
which has been instilled on our popular culture since kindergarten.

32
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,300
Shelly: I don't think Debbie understands what you mean.

33
00:01:51,660 --> 00:01:54,520
Carol: Every year, it's the same chosen few that get nominated.

34
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:56,700
The in crowd, the A list, the sociees.

35
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:00,420
And I'm talking about people whose biggest contribution to this school

36
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:01,600
is looking good in a sweater.

37
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:04,680
Principle: Maybe if you spent less time in the teacher's lounge stuffing

38
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,980
your face with doughnuts, you'd find it... Okee Dokee.

39
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:12,160
Candidates meet in the auditorium after school for briefing.

40
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:17,020
First the candidates for Queen, in alphabetical order: Joya Barnes.

41
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:23,740
Carol: And who's the girl in the tight sweater who always forgets to wear

42
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:24,040
a bra?

43
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:25,940
Principle: Jennifer Calestino.

44
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:30,017
Carol: That's her. And we must have a cheerleader or two.

45
00:02:30,017 --> 00:02:31,019
Principle: Suzanne Fryman.

46
00:02:31,019 --> 00:02:33,018
Carol: One.

47
00:02:33,018 --> 00:02:34,018
Principle: Heather Macombe.

48
00:02:34,018 --> 00:02:36,024
Carol: Two.

49
00:02:36,024 --> 00:02:39,024
Debbie: So you are saying that only the most popular kids get nominated?

50
00:02:39,024 --> 00:02:40,034
Carol: Exactly.

51
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:41,980
Principle: And Carol Seaver.

52
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,960
Carol: Another case and point. What?

53
00:02:49,046 --> 00:03:52,143
Shelly: I'll bet you are sorry now you let your thighs go to hell.

54
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:56,220
Debbie: I've never been best friends with someone in the in crowd before.

55
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:57,820
Carol: I'm not in the in crowd.

56
00:03:58,020 --> 00:03:59,320
Debbie: As soon as we've finished having this picture taken,

57
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,340
we are going to go to Chadwick's and we're going to pick you out a dress.

58
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:02,900
Shelly: Only dogs shop at Chadwick's.

59
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:04,140
Debbie: I shop at Chadwick's.

60
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:06,169
Shelly: Exactly. They don't have a single dress there that shows any bosom.

61
00:04:06,169 --> 00:04:08,166
Debbie: What does that matter?

62
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:10,320
Shelly: For you, not much.

63
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:12,760
But Carol wants to be queen, and when you're going for votes,

64
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:14,460
a little bosom goes a long way.

65
00:04:15,183 --> 00:04:19,188
(dream scene)

66
00:04:19,188 --> 00:04:22,189
Principle: We are missing a candidate. Where's the other girl?

67
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:24,120
Carol: Right here Mr. Dewitt.

68
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:29,940
Principle: You? Ha ha ha. You can't be a queen candidate.

69
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:36,120
You're not showing any bosom. Carol Seaver.

70
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:42,980
Carol: No, no bosom.

71
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:47,460
Principle: Ok. Care to join us Miss Seaver.

72
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:53,540
Now remember people, that the student body looks up to you.

73
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:56,060
So no crossed eyes, or obscene gestures.

74
00:04:56,760 --> 00:05:00,180
Carol: (in her head) I'm in the homecoming court. Me, Carol-the brain-Seaver.

75
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:02,255
How am I ever going to face mum and dad?

76
00:05:02,255 --> 00:05:05,259
(dream scene)

77
00:05:05,259 --> 00:05:07,257
Carol: Hi

78
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:10,880
Jason: Honey, the best and brightest of our children is home.

79
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:14,320
Maggie: You mean the one who gets a consistent four point 0 average,

80
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:15,560
is a member of the chess club,

81
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:19,280
the future physicists of America and is the daughter I vicariously live

82
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:20,820
my life through. That child?

83
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:23,360
Jason: That's the one.

84
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:27,560
Maggie: Well let me just put this darn freelance article I'm writing aside.

85
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:30,240
Jason: I can stuff my duck anytime.

86
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:34,303
Maggie: Carol, tell us what startling achievements you made at school today?

87
00:05:34,303 --> 00:05:40,307
Carol: Mum, dad, I have some news that might be dramatic for you.

88
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:44,400
Jason: Young lady, if you've gone and won the Nobel prize and didn't call us,

89
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:45,460
you're in big trouble.

90
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:47,323
Carol: No, I didn't.

91
00:05:47,323 --> 00:05:50,330
Jason: Ah, who cares. You are a joy to parent anyway.

92
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:52,420
Carol: I know.

93
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,700
Maggie: A devoted sibling.

94
00:05:53,780 --> 00:05:54,480
Carol: I know.

95
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:55,900
Jason: A credit to this nation.

96
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,120
Carol: Dad, you're being a sycophant.

97
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,100
Jason: Thank you.

98
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:01,320
Maggie: Carol, would you please tell me what a sycophant is.

99
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:08,420
Carol: Later mum. See, today I was nominated for home coming queen.

100
00:06:10,362 --> 00:06:14,361
Jason and Maggie: (crying)

101
00:06:14,361 --> 00:06:15,370
Mike: Boy it's foggy in here.

102
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:19,220
Maggie: Mike, you're our best hope now.

103
00:06:19,370 --> 00:06:23,383
Jason: Promise us you'll never become home coming queen.

104
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:30,240
Mike: Dad, it's an electric oven. What the heck is going on around here?

105
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:33,660
Carol: I've been nominated for homecoming queen.

106
00:06:35,402 --> 00:06:41,403
Mike: Hey, that's tough. So is it like a circus theme this year?

107
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:45,420
Ben: Cheese, cheese, cheese. I need cheese to go with my rack of ribs.

108
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:49,422
Hey didn't any of you people hear what I need?

109
00:06:49,422 --> 00:06:52,423
Homecoming girls: Cheese!

110
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:54,300
Photographer: That girl didn't smile.

111
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:58,460
Principle: Miss Seaver, could you be happy for just a moment?

112
00:06:59,940 --> 00:07:00,436
Carol: How's that?

113
00:07:00,436 --> 00:07:02,436
Principle: Fine.

114
00:07:02,820 --> 00:07:06,020
Jason: Ok Chris. I got your diapers, your wipes, your lotion, your bottle,

115
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:10,120
your rattle, your salt, your pepper...nah! You don't need those do you?

116
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:12,120
Anything else you need?

117
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:13,380
Mike: Dad, can I borrow some money?

118
00:07:13,455 --> 00:07:17,461
Jason: Pardon. Mike, no.

119
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,800
Mike: Oh come on dad. Just twenty bucks till Friday.

120
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:21,466
I mean if you ever need a favour, you got it.

121
00:07:21,466 --> 00:07:22,469
Jason: Only twenty?

122
00:07:22,820 --> 00:07:23,474
Mike: Well actually...

123
00:07:23,474 --> 00:07:25,477
Jason: Twenty is all you're getting.

124
00:07:25,477 --> 00:07:28,482
Mike: Alright, you drive a hard bargain dad.

125
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:30,640
Maggie: Jason we have to hurry.

126
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:32,480
If we are five minutes late for this pediatrician,

127
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:35,440
he'll make us wait an hour. You know how impossible doctors can be?

128
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:36,580
Jason: Yeah, I've heard.

129
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:40,499
Maggie: Oh Jason, Chrissy has to be changed.

130
00:07:40,499 --> 00:07:42,503
Jason: Mike. Favour time.

131
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:50,512
Mike: Oh dad! Alright. Let's get this over with Chrissy.

132
00:07:50,512 --> 00:07:51,513
Carol: Hi.

133
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,380
Maggie: Hi honey. How was school?

134
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:57,320
Carol: Well I might as well get this over with.

135
00:07:58,940 --> 00:08:00,440
Mum, dad, can I talk to the two of you.

136
00:08:00,527 --> 00:08:01,536
Maggie: Well of course sweet heart.

137
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,580
Carol: Maybe you better sit.

138
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:05,080
Jason: Carol, is this serious?

139
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,400
Carol: I'm afraid so.

140
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:11,560
Now I know that both have always thought of me as the sensible one.

141
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:15,320
Your one child with her head on the ground and feet out of the clouds.

142
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:21,720
No that's wrong. Anyway, you can well imagine how I felt today when,

143
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:26,140
when I found out that, that I was nominated for home coming queen.

144
00:08:26,572 --> 00:08:27,574
Jason: Holy cow, that is...

145
00:08:27,574 --> 00:08:30,580
Maggie: Carol, that is wonderful.

146
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:34,940
Carol: Congratulations! Dad, I'm being lumped in with cheerleader.

147
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:39,700
Jason: Uh hu. Well some of my favorite people are cheerleaders.

148
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:42,240
Carol: But all the other nominees are just pretty and popular.

149
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:45,100
Maggie: Well honey, what's wrong with that?

150
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:49,680
Carol: Wrong. Mum, people in the homecoming court are never people of

151
00:08:49,680 --> 00:08:53,060
consequence. Do you think mother Theresa was a homecoming queen?

152
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,160
Jason: Oh, you know for a fact that she wasn't?

153
00:08:57,200 --> 00:09:00,580
Carol: Alright, alright. So we'll take mum for example. She'd never be part of something

154
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:01,560
silly like this

155
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:04,980
Maggie: Well actually I was homecoming queen.

156
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:07,400
Carol: That explains so much.

157
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:11,440
Maggie: Carol you can be a person of substance and still be popular and

158
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:11,840
pretty.

159
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:14,440
Carol: You're not talking about Evana White, are you?

160
00:09:14,780 --> 00:09:15,660
Jason: There you go.

161
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:18,300
Carol: Can't you see.

162
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:23,080
The people who voted to nominate me don't know who or what I am.

163
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:23,820
Jason: And what's that?

164
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:26,260
Carol: My own father doesn't know what I am.

165
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,280
Jason: Well do you know what you are?

166
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:29,300
Maggie: Oh Jason, just tell her what she is.

167
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:32,740
Mike: I'd be happy to do it. There you go dad.

168
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:36,040
Believe me, I earned that twenty bucks. And some change.

169
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:39,200
Maggie: Carol honey, this is wonderful news.

170
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:41,460
There is nothing here for you to get upset about.

171
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:42,100
Mike: What news?

172
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:43,760
Jason: Not now Mike.

173
00:09:43,860 --> 00:09:46,840
Carol: No, no. It's alright. I'd like to hear what Mike has to say.

174
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:52,620
Mike, I've been nominated for home coming queen.

175
00:09:53,709 --> 00:09:55,714
Mike: What this is some kind of joke, right?

176
00:09:55,714 --> 00:09:57,714
Carol: No.

177
00:09:57,714 --> 00:10:01,725
Mike: So like is it a circus theme this year?

178
00:10:01,725 --> 00:10:10,732
Carol: Thank you. Mike. A lonely fool speaks the truth.

179
00:10:10,732 --> 00:10:18,747
(Carol's dream)

180
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:20,180
Girl: Thank you Mr. Dewitt.

181
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:21,900
Thank you my family,

182
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:26,020
my friends and those of you who dream of being my friends.

183
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:30,720
Thank you everyone who clings unto my prize bosom.

184
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:35,860
I couldn't be the regular gal I am without you.

185
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:40,820
Principle: What a lovely, all be it empty, sentiment.

186
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:50,580
Last and certainly least, Carol Seaver.

187
00:10:52,799 --> 00:10:53,806
Carol: Enough bosom for you Shelly?

188
00:10:53,806 --> 00:10:55,806
Shelly: Good and plenty.

189
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:57,809
Debbie: Lovely, lovely, lovely.

190
00:10:57,809 --> 00:10:59,810
Principle: Carol Seaver, we're waiting.

191
00:11:00,340 --> 00:11:05,000
Carol: How do I look? Oh no. You!

192
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:08,180
You think you are in the same league as these people? Ha!

193
00:11:08,830 --> 00:11:14,837
Principle: Now Seaver. Move it! Don't!

194
00:11:14,837 --> 00:11:29,857
Everyone: (laughing)

195
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:40,600
Mike: Ladies and gentlemen. If you will direct your attention to the centre ring, and feast your eyes on the largest woman in the great state of New York. Don't

196
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:44,600
be alarmed. She is merely going through a stage

197
00:11:51,889 --> 00:11:53,899
(alarm clock)

198
00:11:54,260 --> 00:11:56,540
Carol: That's one stage I'm never going through.

199
00:12:02,906 --> 00:12:03,914
Mike: Hey! Morning, dad.

200
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:07,260
Jason: Hi mike. You're up bright and early this morning.

201
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:10,180
Mike: Yeah, well the noise of you cooking bacon and eggs woke me.

202
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,900
Jason: I'll try to be more careful next time.

203
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:16,100
Mike: You know, to tell you the truth dad, I was up early to study,

204
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:19,820
and well I was going to make breakfast but I ran out of crackers.

205
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:25,140
Jason: Mike, you want some breakfast? Mike!

206
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:29,600
Mike: Oh wow. You know it never occurred to me to impose on you guys.

207
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:34,720
Morning, mum.

208
00:12:34,956 --> 00:12:35,959
Maggie: Morning.

209
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:37,840
Mike: You guys are great feeding me like this.

210
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:38,966
Maggie: Put down your fork, this is Carol's.

211
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:38,971
Mike: What?

212
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:42,300
Jason: Well I didn't know you'd be joining us for breakfast Mike,

213
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:44,620
so I didn't cook you any eggs. But there is plenty of cereal.

214
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:46,980
Mike: Cereal, you guys invited me in here for cereal?

215
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:48,986
Jason: Well crackers if you prefer.

216
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:51,960
Ben: Hey Mike, you want the shiny part of my bacon?

217
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:53,960
Jason: Carol's not down yet?

218
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:55,320
Maggie: No. She's still not herself.

219
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:57,400
Ben: I love it when Carol's in the dumper.

220
00:12:57,996 --> 00:13:01,620
Carol: Good morning mum, dad, Ben and Michael.

221
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:03,560
Maggie: Honey, how are you?

222
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:05,500
Carol: I'm sitting on top of the world.

223
00:13:06,140 --> 00:13:07,060
Mike: Look out Iceland.

224
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:09,460
Jason: Enough Mike.

225
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:10,880
Carol: No, that was funny.

226
00:13:11,014 --> 00:13:12,017
Ben: What?

227
00:13:12,017 --> 00:13:14,018
Carol: What Mike said? It was funny.

228
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:15,620
Mike: It was a fat joke.

229
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:16,029
Carol: I know.

230
00:13:16,029 --> 00:13:18,028
Ben: What the heck's going on here?

231
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:21,060
Maggie: Usually you find Mikes jokes anything but funny.

232
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:23,660
Ben: But funny. That's a hot one mum.

233
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:29,860
Carol: Well last night I had an insightful vision.

234
00:13:29,860 --> 00:13:32,600
I'm cool, I'm calm, and my course is set.

235
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:35,800
I know exactly what I have to do and how I'm going to do it.

236
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:38,140
All my energy is directed into one purpose,

237
00:13:38,140 --> 00:13:40,480
and I have none to spare for distractions.

238
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:43,760
And certainly not the primal ramblings of this pimple faced pus bag.

239
00:13:45,073 --> 00:13:50,076
Mike: That's better.

240
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:51,640
Shelly: Carol, where have you been?

241
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:54,100
You only have five minutes to make yourself presentable. Go!

242
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:56,800
Carol: I was talking to Mr. Zurich about the fall of the Roman Empire.

243
00:13:57,280 --> 00:13:58,760
Debbie: Fall of the Roman Empire?

244
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:01,100
We've got an election here, and you are thinking about Caesar.

245
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:04,100
Carol: I thought a lot about this home coming stuff.

246
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:06,540
Shelly: I brought all my shades.

247
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:09,540
Debbie: Shelly, making Carol look like a tramp,

248
00:14:09,540 --> 00:14:10,109
is not the way to go about this.

249
00:14:10,109 --> 00:14:11,113
Carol: And I've decided...

250
00:14:11,113 --> 00:14:12,109
Shelly: Tramp!

251
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:13,117
Carol: After much rational thought.

252
00:14:13,117 --> 00:14:14,120
Debbie: Here. Use my blusher.

253
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:16,118
Carol: And a highly symbolic dream.

254
00:14:16,118 --> 00:14:17,124
Shelly: Is this what you are wearing right now?

255
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:19,260
Debbie: It sure is.

256
00:14:20,126 --> 00:14:22,129
Carol: That my only course of action is...

257
00:14:22,129 --> 00:14:24,128
Debbie and Shelly: No make up!

258
00:14:24,128 --> 00:14:25,133
Carol: Right. How did you guess?

259
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:26,720
Shelly: Are you nuts?

260
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:30,340
Carol: no, I'm realistic. And I know I don't belong with these people.

261
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:31,660
Shelly: Neither do we.

262
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:36,580
Carol: And when my name is called today, I'm going to decline the nomination.

263
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:38,620
Debbie: You are nuts.

264
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:41,820
Carol: Nope. I just know what I am.

265
00:14:43,163 --> 00:14:46,163
Debbie: We were this close to royalty.

266
00:14:46,540 --> 00:14:50,160
Shelly: Yeah. Till you showed her the make up you got from clown school.

267
00:14:52,178 --> 00:14:54,175
Girl in red: Did you here that?

268
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:56,760
Girl in blue: Carol Seaver's going for the natural look.

269
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:59,420
Girl in green: It's the old humble bit. Act like you don't care at all.

270
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:01,400
Girl in yellow: What a cheap way to get votes.

271
00:15:07,195 --> 00:15:15,209
All: Hmmm.

272
00:15:15,209 --> 00:15:23,220
Principle: Dewey Highs finest. The rest of you could learn from their example. How many people did you pull from that burning building Gareth?

273
00:15:23,220 --> 00:15:24,226
Gareth: Twenty four, sir.

274
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:27,900
Principle: Did you hear that? Hu? Sir.

275
00:15:30,260 --> 00:15:32,720
Turning our attention now to some more fine Hooters,

276
00:15:33,780 --> 00:15:36,300
the candidates for homecoming queen.

277
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:42,640
All visions of loveliness and what the hell happened to you?

278
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:46,660
Carol: Mr. Dewitt. I respectfully decline my nomination.

279
00:15:46,860 --> 00:15:47,620
Principle: What? You can't.

280
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:50,100
Girl 1: I respectfully decline my nomination too.

281
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:51,140
Principle: The head cheerleader?

282
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:51,700
Girl 2: Me too.

283
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:52,273
Other girls: So do we.

284
00:15:52,273 --> 00:15:57,277
Shelly and Debbie: We'll do it. We'll do it.

285
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:02,840
Principle: Get away. Get away. You girls will resign over my dead body.

286
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,520
Got that? Let go of it.

287
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:10,160
Carol: Well if they won't let me decline their stupid nomination,

288
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:12,540
I just won't go to their stupid dance tonight.

289
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,160
Maggie: Why is it stupid?

290
00:16:14,307 --> 00:16:17,304
Carol: They are trying to rub my nose in it.

291
00:16:17,620 --> 00:16:18,314
Maggie: Rub your nose in what?

292
00:16:18,314 --> 00:16:21,317
Carol: The fact that they are so perfect.

293
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:25,220
Maggie: Carol, it sounds to me like you are afraid that they are better

294
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:26,320
than you are.

295
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:30,300
Carol: Well obviously you have not heard a word I've said,

296
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:33,460
and it's a waste of time to talk to a former homecoming queen.

297
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:35,900
Maggie: Don't take that tone with me young lady,

298
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:37,780
or you'll be grounded and you won't go to that dance.

299
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,780
Carol: That's what I want mum. Ground me.

300
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,440
Maggie: Absolutely not. Now go to your room and don't come out.

301
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:51,364
Except to go to the dance. And you. You wait till now to come in?

302
00:16:51,364 --> 00:16:53,363
Jason: Oh, you said you wanted to handle it.

303
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:54,860
Maggie: And you listen to me?

304
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:01,240
Jason: Brought you a little snack.

305
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:03,384
Carol: What's the matter, I'm not fat enough for you?

306
00:17:03,384 --> 00:17:13,400
Jason: Oh no. You are plenty f...Oh no. You know what I mean. Is this the homecoming dress that you are not going to wear?

307
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:15,398
Carol: You're not going to get me to go to that dance.

308
00:17:15,398 --> 00:17:17,404
Jason: Hey, you make your own decisions. I respect them.

309
00:17:18,060 --> 00:17:19,260
Carol: Thank you.

310
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:23,620
Jason: Not like you are a little girl anymore. Like in this picture.

311
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:27,640
What was this ribbon? Second grade spelling B.

312
00:17:28,320 --> 00:17:30,320
Carol: Yes, Y E S, yes.

313
00:17:31,340 --> 00:17:33,940
Jason: Cute. Same sense of humour as your mother.

314
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:37,860
Carol: She thinks I should go and have a pleasant memory.

315
00:17:38,620 --> 00:17:42,960
Jason: Hey, no pressure here. Ahhh, your happy camper medal.

316
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:43,444
Do you remember that?

317
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:45,140
Carol: Barely. I was seven.

318
00:17:46,340 --> 00:17:49,240
Jason: Remember how your mum and I had to drag you kicking and screaming

319
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,740
to your first happy camper meeting. Hu?

320
00:17:51,060 --> 00:17:53,240
Carol: Dad, with all due respect, do you have a point,

321
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:54,340
or are you just babbling?

322
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:59,980
Jason: Just babbling. Oh look, oh there you are with your glasses on.

323
00:17:59,980 --> 00:18:03,000
And what was that? Two years ago. I don't even recognize that girl.

324
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:05,040
Carol: It's me.

325
00:18:05,580 --> 00:18:10,200
Jason: I guess the days of overalls and baby fat are gone now.

326
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:14,020
This is not the Carol Seaver I know anymore.

327
00:18:14,493 --> 00:18:18,500
Carol: Dad, that is not babbling, that's a point.

328
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:22,120
Jason: Well I just wanted to take a little trip down memory lane,

329
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:26,560
to see how my little girl had grown up into such an incredibly beautiful

330
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:38,020
woman. You know, things happen so fast sometimes that we forget to see

331
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:42,500
the changes in a person. In ourselves.

332
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:45,420
Carol: I liked it better when you were just babbling.

333
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:47,740
Jason: You are just like your mum.

334
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:53,500
Carol: Mike, insult me.

335
00:18:53,552 --> 00:18:55,552
Mike: What, don't you knock? What, were you raised in a barn?

336
00:18:55,580 --> 00:18:56,660
Carol: That's not an insult.

337
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:57,900
Mike: What is this?

338
00:18:58,160 --> 00:19:01,020
Carol: Come on. I was counting on you treating me like you always have.

339
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:01,920
Mike: And how's that?

340
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:05,240
Carol: Like scum. Now come on. How about a fat joke for old times sake.

341
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:10,582
Mike: A fat joke. Alright uh. Ok uh. Well I'd ask you to sit down, but...

342
00:19:10,582 --> 00:19:11,582
Carol: Yeah.

343
00:19:11,582 --> 00:19:13,589
Mike: Now come on. You're taking all the fun out of this Carol.

344
00:19:13,589 --> 00:19:15,587
Carol: Ok, the how about a nerd joke.

345
00:19:15,587 --> 00:19:16,591
Mike: Ok. A nerd joke, great.

346
00:19:16,591 --> 00:19:17,593
Carol: I won't help you.

347
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:22,020
Mike: Ok. Well I'd ask you to sit down, but... Oh no.

348
00:19:22,020 --> 00:19:25,460
That was my fat joke. I'm loosing it, I'm loosing it. Um,

349
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:28,600
Carol: Come on Mike. You can do it. I need one insult.

350
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:31,160
You're the only person I know who won't lie to me.

351
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:33,140
Mike: I don't do well under pressure Carol.

352
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:34,619
Carol: I know. I've seen your grades.

353
00:19:34,619 --> 00:19:36,619
Mike: Ok, who's supposed to be doing the insults here?

354
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:39,280
Carol: You are weenie. Now come on! Think.

355
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:43,260
Think blimps, pigs, wide body tires.

356
00:19:43,634 --> 00:19:44,637
Mike: Tires?

357
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:48,180
Carol: Brains, four eyes, nerds, geeks.

358
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:50,900
Mike: Alright, alright, you're not a nerd and you're not fat anymore.

359
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:52,060
What do you want from me?

360
00:19:52,220 --> 00:19:54,880
Carol: Oh, and the next thing you are going to say is that I'm part of

361
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:56,580
the in crowd and the A list and the sociees.

362
00:19:57,220 --> 00:19:58,920
Mike: well of course you are. Everybody knows that.

363
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:02,660
Carol: Oh thanks Mike. Thanks for nothing.

364
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:06,860
Mike: Well alright. You know, you've got one humungous uh...uh...

365
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:12,720
And with a face like yours, you could...uh...Oh no, it's gone.

366
00:20:22,691 --> 00:20:26,702
Carol: It is going to be a circus theme this year.

367
00:20:26,840 --> 00:20:27,960
Girl in red: Great dress.

368
00:20:28,820 --> 00:20:29,708
Carol: You're talking to me?

369
00:20:29,708 --> 00:20:31,707
Girl in red: Yeah.

370
00:20:31,707 --> 00:20:33,714
Carol: Well thank you.

371
00:20:33,714 --> 00:20:36,714
Both together: I'm so nervous.

372
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:37,760
Both together: You're nervous?

373
00:20:39,510 --> 00:20:43,800
Carol: What do you know? Oh Jennifer, you look radiant.

374
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:46,900
Jennifer: Thank you. I have to throw up.

375
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,240
Carol: She's nervous too.

376
00:20:52,738 --> 00:20:53,745
Girl in blue: I know what you are thinking.

377
00:20:53,745 --> 00:20:54,746
Carol: What?

378
00:20:55,060 --> 00:20:56,380
Girl in blue: That I don't belong here.

379
00:20:56,900 --> 00:20:58,260
Carol: Oh no. No.

380
00:20:58,747 --> 00:21:03,761
Girl in blue: Well, you are right.

381
00:21:03,950 --> 00:21:05,460
Girl in pink: What are you smiling at?

382
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:09,700
Carol: I'm getting the feeling that nobody thinks they belong here.

383
00:21:10,180 --> 00:21:12,000
Girl in pink: Not everybody is in your league,

384
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,880
but you don't have to rub our noses in it.

385
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:15,380
Carol: Not in my league?

386
00:21:15,773 --> 00:21:17,300
Girl in pink: Oh come on. You are in all the clubs.

387
00:21:17,340 --> 00:21:19,100
You got great grades, great hair.

388
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:28,780
Girl in red: This is it!

389
00:21:29,020 --> 00:21:30,800
Jennifer: Oh no. Not again.

390
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:33,740
Guy: Get ready people.

391
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:37,600
Principle: I present the homecoming court.

392
00:21:39,500 --> 00:21:41,200
Girl in pink: We can't leave without Jennifer.

393
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,460
Girl in red: Oh yes, we can.

394
00:21:42,816 --> 00:21:57,440
Principle: Do you people need a telegram? Let's move it, move it, move it!

395
00:21:57,440 --> 00:21:58,720
Carol's man: We're supposed to go now.

396
00:21:58,760 --> 00:21:59,500
Carol: In a minute.

397
00:21:59,980 --> 00:22:00,600
Carol's man: In a minute!

398
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:07,800
Carol: It's really me.

399
00:22:08,100 --> 00:22:10,040
Carol's man: Uh hu. Are you having a nervous breakdown or something?

400
00:22:10,861 --> 00:22:36,900
Carol: Nope. I already had it. Let's go.

401
00:22:36,900 --> 00:22:43,914
Jason: Here she is.

402
00:22:43,914 --> 00:22:45,916
Carol: Hello.

403
00:22:45,916 --> 00:22:46,016
Maggie: Hi honey. How was the dance?

404
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:49,920
Carol: Wonderful.

405
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:50,020
Jason: Well, did you win the, uh? Are you the new, uh? You had a good time?

406
00:22:54,934 --> 00:22:55,936
Carol: Perfect.

407
00:22:55,936 --> 00:22:56,036
Maggie: And the homecoming court was?

408
00:22:57,935 --> 00:22:59,935
Carol: Magnificent.

409
00:22:59,935 --> 00:23:00,035
Maggie: Oh Carol, did you?

410
00:23:00,035 --> 00:23:02,340
Carol: No. Heather McDonald did. But we all got roses and a big gold bracelet.

411
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:04,220
Jason: Oh, that's beautiful.

412
00:23:04,220 --> 00:23:04,980
Maggie: Oh, that's wonderful.

413
00:23:05,780 --> 00:23:12,220
Carol: And mum, you were right. It will be a wonderful memory. Night.

414
00:23:17,963 --> 00:23:18,965
Maggie: Night.

415
00:23:19,540 --> 00:23:22,520
Mike: Oh, Carol, I need you. Alright. Here, are you ready for this? Here it comes. So, like, did they make a triple sized throne for you

416
00:23:22,520 --> 00:23:24,460
Carol: Thank you Mike. That was very sweet.

417
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:29,520
Mike: I knew it. I am losing it.
